hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1110","From Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawrqi, from Marhum, meaning Ibn Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq, on the authority of Ibn Umar, He said: I was with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and a Bedouin one night, and the Bedouin said: O Messenger of God, how is the night prayer? Then he, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Two by two, so if you fear dawn, prostrate one prostration, and prostrate two prostrations before the morning prayer.”"
